course: dictionary
lesson: 15077
title: Rigorous: careful and strict
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Rigorous means very careful, thorough and exact. A rigorous check looks at every part, step by step, so nothing gets missed.
explain: Rigorous can also mean strict or hard. «The team had rigorous training every morning before school.» The training was tough, and it was meant to make the players stronger.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The scientists did rigorous testing.» Does careful testing fit? Yes, so rigorous means careful and thorough here.
fact: Rigorous means very careful, thorough and exact.
fact: Rigorous can also mean strict or hard, like rigorous training.
fact: Rigorous is an adjective: rigorous, more rigorous, most rigorous.
fact: Useful phrases are rigorous testing and a rigorous check.
fact: In science and maths, a rigorous proof checks every single step.
exercise: «The scientists ran rigorous tests before they shared their results.» What does rigorous mean here? | Quick and messy | Funny | Loud and busy | *Very careful and thorough
exercise: «The coach set a rigorous training plan for the team.» What does rigorous suggest? | Quiet | *Tough and strict | Silly | Short and easy
exercise: Which phrase means a check that looks at every detail? | a quick glance | a funny story | a loud noise | *a rigorous check
test: A doctor gives her patient a rigorous examination. Which word is closest in meaning to rigorous? | Loud and proud | *Careful and thorough | Happy and calm | Careless and quick
test: Ella says rigorous means cheap. Why is she wrong? | It means very old | It means very wet | It means cheap and small | *It is about how careful or strict something is, not the price
exam: «Only a rigorous proof will convince the judges.» What does rigorous mean? | *Careful and exact, checking every step | Coloured | Sleepy | Careless
